From b12ddefeb90c81d735a8a93b25999d78d8dceef2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 03:22:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] REVIEW-2 fixes: three defects in the REVIEW-1 fixes (hourly
 review loop on aff4167 / fa06b9f).
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. (critical) MyPLC_IO_Modbus.cpp:286: the W906_SafePlcFrameMark call sat AFTER the line's existing `//完成過一次` comment, so it was never compiled -> the link-lost alarm fired 2 s after every START with a healthy PLC. Test [7] called the mark directly and stayed green. Now the call is before the comment, and "lost" = socket not connected or 2 requests in a row unanswered within hCheckTime (1 s) (W906_SafePlcFrameMiss on the timeout branch, same line; reset on a reply) -- a 2 s tick stall no longer blames the PLC. Test [7] now drives the real PLCIOTaskCycle (send, two 1.1 s timeouts, a reply): 75/75. All 11,128 lines added today scanned for code after a `//`: 0 (control: the bad line is caught).
2. (high) Pci1203Monitor.cpp: heartbeat stamped GetTickCount()|1u could be 1 ms ahead of "now" -> the unsigned difference wrapped -> RunSync refused normal requests incl. STOPs at random; and the heartbeat-based freeze clock refused STOPs during a long but alive Poll. RunSync's immediate refusal and heartbeat-based clock are reverted (original behaviour); stamp is `t ? t : 1`; EOF W906_Pci1203IoHeartAgeMs (signed); only WebMotorAccessLive.cpp W906_TorqueFocus (the every-beat torque SDO focus) skips itself when the heartbeat is >= 5 s old.
3. (medium) WAR16155 is RULINGS_20261005 #96's "1203 card command failed" -> the safety-PLC link-lost alarm is WAR16156 (csystem.cpp same line; AlarmCodeList.txt; web tables in the web commit).

Debug + release (affected targets). WORKLOG section 2 row 143.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
